Sanitation Associate

Shifts -1st 4:00am to 2:30pm, 2nd 2:15pm to 12:45am, 3rd 8:00pm to 6:30am

&nbsp;

Factor_ a brand of HelloFresh is seeking a Sanitation Associates.&nbsp; The Sanitation Associate is responsible for all the activities involved in maintaining cleanliness and a food safe environment in production areas, surrounding areas and equipment.

&nbsp;

Essential Functions:

• Responsible for cleaning and sanitation of all food production equipment and machinery. I.E. Production machines, tables, mats, compost bins, sinks, drains, walls, and any surface that is scheduled for sanitation duties.&nbsp;

• Responsible for cleaning and sanitizing all kitting and packing equipment and surfaces.

• May be required to operate the dish-machine as needed.&nbsp;

• Restocks all PPE as needed, such as hairnets, beard nets, gloves, face masks, and sleeve guards.&nbsp;

• Responsible for the assistance in inventory of all linens/uniforms.

• Responsible for all chemicals, their use, and safe handling.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Document all job duties performed with work logs and follows the master schedule as directed.

• Perform other tasks as directed by supervisor/managers.&nbsp;

• Must follow all SSOP’s and Safety Regulations.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Regular and timely attendance.

Work Environment: This is a cold, wet, environment with exposure to chemicals that requires standing, lifting, reaching, and twisting for 8 hours or until the job is completed.

• The employee may be exposed to fumes or airborne food particles and allergens, moving mechanical parts and vibration&nbsp;

• The employee will be responsible for using chemicals at safe-handling concentrations along with appropriate PPE

Physical Demands:

• While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to stand, walk, stoop, reach and lift for 10 hours with or without reasonable accommodation&nbsp;

• The employee is required to use hands to handle, or feel objects and/or tools

• The employee must regularly lift and move up to 25 pounds, and occasionally lift and move up to 50 pounds with or without assistance

At a Minimum, you have:

• Ability to read and write English, follow verbal instructions and use simple math

• Must be at least 18 years old

• Basic computer skills preferred

• Highschool diploma or GED

This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the responsibilities. However, the Company reserves the right to adjust, modify, or reassign work tasks and responsibilities as needed to meet changing business needs, operational requirements, or other factors.

